# --- Secrets: never commit these ---
# NOTE: gitignore has no inline comments -- a trailing "# ..." becomes part of
# the pattern and silently matches nothing. Keep comments on their own line.

# SSH: whitelist, not blacklist. Only `config` is tracked, so no key or
# host-state file can slip in under a name the patterns did not anticipate.
ssh/.ssh/*
!ssh/.ssh/config

# gh CLI auth token lives here
**/.config/gh/hosts.yml

**/.netrc
**/*token*
**/*secret*
**/*.key
**/*.pem

# --- IDE / app caches & state (machine/version specific) ---
JetBrains/
DataGripProjects/
**/.idea/
**/*.iml

# --- Editor / tooling junk ---
**/.claude/
# macOS Finder metadata
**/.DS_Store
**/.cache/
**/*.swp
**/*.bak

# --- Yazi caches ---
yazi/.config/yazi/.claude/
